<h1>English Subcategorization  Grammar for Natural Language Generation</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 1:11 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>Y0</b><br />AVALENT<br /><br /><b>Y1</b><br />NO SUBCATEGORIZATION FRAME: rules defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>Y31</b><br />Intransitive verb (<i>calcify, bifurcate, dissolve</i>)<br />VS(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y32</b><br />Intransitive verb (<i>walk away, make peace, kill oneself</i>)<br />VS(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y33</b><br />Intransitive verb whose subject is a dummy pronoun (<i>snow, thunder</i>)<br />VS(DUM);<br /><br /><b>Y34</b><br />Indirect transitive verb (<i>begin, contribute</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(VH(INF))VC(PP);<br /><br /><b>Y35</b><br />Direct transitive verb with a complement (<i>make (me happy)</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(NP);VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(JP);<br /><br /><b>Y36</b><br />Intransitive verb with a complement (<i>drive (crazy)</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);VS(NP)VC(JP);<br /><br /><b>Y37</b><br />Intransitive verb with a complement (<i>think (big)</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(JP);<br /><br /><b>Y38</b><br />Direct transitive verb (<i>accept, accomplish, acknowledge</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y39</b><br />Direct transitive verb (<i>importune, impress, intimidate</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y40</b><br />Direct transitive verb (<i>rejuvenate, scare, strike</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y41</b><br />Direct transitive verb (<i>account for, add, assimilate</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y42</b><br />Indirect transitive verb that selects the preposition "to" (<i>appeal, pertain</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y43</b><br />Indirect transitive verb that selects the preposition "on" (<i>concentrate, focus</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PH([on]));<br /><br /><b>Y44</b><br />Ditransitive verb that takes two direct objects (<i>address, allow, call</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y45</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "to" (<i>commit, give</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y46</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "from" (<i>extort, keep back</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([from]));<br /><br /><b>Y47</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "with" (<i>empower, familiarise</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([with]));<br /><br /><b>Y48</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "of" (<i>absolve, deprive</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([of]));<br /><br /><b>Y49</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "on" (<i>impose, inflict</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([on]));<br /><br /><b>Y50</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by a preposition (<i>accustom, compensate</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PP);<br /><br /><b>Y51</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by a preposition (<i>classify, conciliate, place</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PP);<br /><br /><b>Y52</b><br />Indirect transitive verb (<i>come, cope, deal</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PP);<br /><br /><b>Y53</b><br />Intransitive verb (<i>suppurate, necrose</i>)<br />VS(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y54</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is a clause (<i>designate, exhort</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PC([to];VH(INF)));<br /><br /><b>Y55</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is a clause (<i>induce, invite</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(VH(INF));<br /><br /><b>Y56</b><br />Direct transitive verb whose object is a clause (<i>anticipate, argue, ascertain</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(CH([that]));<br /><br /><b>Y57</b><br />Indirect transitive verb that selects the preposition "to" (<i>submit, give in</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y58</b><br />Indirect itransitive verb whose indirect object is a clause (<i>come close, fail</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PH([to];VH(INF)));<br /><br /><b>Y59</b><br />Direct transitive verb whose object is a clause (<i>check, wonder</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(CC([whether];VH(INF)));<br /><br /><b>Y60</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is a clause introduced by "into" (<i>persuade, shame</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PC([into];VH(GER)));<br /><br /><b>Y61</b><br />Ditransitive verb whose indirect object is introduced by "with" (<i>combine, unite</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP)VC(PH([with]));<br /><br /><b>Y62</b><br />Direct transitive verb whose object is a clause (<i>dare, presume</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(VH(INF));<br /><br /><b>Y63</b><br />Direct transitive verb whose object is a clause (<i>avoid, go along</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(VH(GER));<br /><br /><b>Y64</b><br />Direct transitive verb whose object is a clause and the subject is a dummy pronoun (<i>appear, seem</i>)<br />VS(DUM)VC(CH([that]));<br /><br /><b>Y65</b><br />Indirect itransitive verb whose indirect object is a clause (<i>allow, let</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(VH(INF));<br /><br /><b>Y76</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "of" (<i>intention, lack, result, smell, taste</i>)<br />NC(PH([of]));<br /><br /><b>Y78</b><br />Adjective requiring complement introduced by "to" (<i>according > according to</i>)<br />JC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y79</b><br />Adjective requiring complement introduced by "with" (<i>consistent > consistent with</i>)<br />JC(PH([with]));<br /><br /><b>Y80</b><br />Adjective requiring complement introduced by "for" (<i>hungry > hungry for</i>)<br />JC(PH([for]));<br /><br /><b>Y81</b><br />Adjective requiring complement introduced by "from" (<i>distinct > distinct from</i>)<br />JC(PH([from]));<br /><br /><b>Y82</b><br />Adjective requiring complement introduced by "of" (<i>capable > capable of</i>)<br />JC(PH([of]));<br /><br /><b>Y83</b><br />Adverb requiring a noun phrase as complement (<i>a.k.a.</i>)<br />AC(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y84</b><br />Adverb requiring a complementizer phrase as complement (<i>much as</i>)<br />AC(CP);<br /><br /><b>Y86</b><br />Adverb requiring complement introduced by "with" (<i>along > along with</i>)<br />AC(PH([with]));<br /><br /><b>Y87</b><br />Adverb requiring complement introduced by "for" (<i>in return > in return for</i>)<br />AC(PH([for]));<br /><br /><b>Y88</b><br />Adverb requiring complement introduced by "on" (<i>up > up on</i>)<br />JC(PH([on]));<br /><br /><b>Y197</b><br />The adverb requires a complement introduced by "to" (<i>fortunately [to him]</i>)<br />AC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y206</b><br />The complement in a complementizer phrase is an inflectional phrase (<i>if [John comes]
</i>)<br />CC(IP);
<br /><br /><b>Y208</b><br />The specifier in an inflectional phrase is a noun phrase and the complement in an inflectional phrase is a verbal phrase (<i>[Mary] will [kiss Peter]</i>)<br />IS(NP)IC(VP);
<br /><br /><b>Y210</b><br />The complement in a noun phrase is a prepositional phrase (<i>construction [of Babel]</i>)<br />NC(PH([of]));
<br /><br /><b>Y247</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "to" (<i>access, alternative, exception, invitation, solution</i>)<br />NC(PH([to]));<br /><br /><b>Y248</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "for" (<i>admiration, credit, desire, hope</i>)<br />NC(PH([for]));<br /><br /><b>Y249</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "on" (<i>attack, authority, effect, expert, influence</i>)<br />NC(PH([on]));<br /><br /><b>Y250</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "in" (<i>decrease, delay, difficulty, experience</i>)<br />NC(PH([in]));<br /><br /><b>Y251</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "between" (<i>comparison, connection, difference</i>)<br />NC(PH([between]));<br /><br /><b>Y252</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "with" (<i>association, contrast, link, relationship</i>)<br />NC(PH([with]));<br /><br /><b>Y253</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "towards" (<i>cruelty</i>)<br />NC(PH([towards]));<br /><br /><b>Y254</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "about" (<i>information, opinion</i>)<br />NC(PH([about]));<br /><br /><b>Y255</b><br />Noun requiring a complement introduced by "from" (<i>protection</i>)<br />NC(PH([from]));<br /><br /><b>Y259</b><br />The complement in a prepositional phrase is a noun phrase (<i>book of [Peter]; book about [Peter]</i>)<br />PC(NP);
